[Music]  it's that time of the month again yet  this time things have changed  playstation plus is now split into three  tiers and today it's all about the free  games we get as playstation plus  essential subscribers that's gonna take  time to get used to this tier now gives  us at least two games a month and this  time there's three so let's do this on  the ps4 and ps5 is crash bandicoot it's  about time the iconic platformer is back  as we are sent to gather the quantum  masks to prevent neocortex from taking  over the multiverse crash 4 mixes up the  old formula by adding new mechanics like  wall running and rail skating but it's  the addition of other characters that  really sets this one apart toner has a  grapple hook for combat and grabbing  boxes that are seemingly impossible to  reach neocortex has a dash mechanic and  a ray gun for battles and the slow dingo  dial has a vacuum to turn crates into  weapons even with the addition of all  these combat related items timing your  jumps remains key to progression and  although the difficulty level is lower  there are flashback missions and mirror  modes for those who like to experience  crash punishment the main reason the  game feels more forgiving is thanks to  one thing there's a shadow under crash  the days of guessing where your  character is are gone reviewers mostly  love crash four with the average score  eight out of ten also on the ps4 is the  dark pictures man of medan i guess we'd  class this as an interactive drama as  the story plays out before us and we  impact that story by making key  decisions man of madan is made by the  same team that brought us until dawn yet  this time it's much more serious than  its predecessor the greatest part of  these games is that each decision has  consequence and two playthroughs of the  same story can yield very different  cutscenes and endings i have to admit  the first 90 minutes of mana madan are  cripplingly slow but it does get better  if you stick around long enough there  are many ways to unalive the heroes of  the story and there's lots of gore so  prepare yourself if you're a little  squeamish one of the most impressive  parts at least to me is the online game  mode jump in with a friend and take  control of a character each and try to  survive your paths cross constantly and  your actions affect what they see do you  team up and coordinate an attack or  completely ignore your teammates the  result can be hilarious and it's much  less scary when you play with a friend  review scores are all over the place for  the dark pictures series 7 out of 10 was  the most consistent i found for man of  madan and our third game for july is  arcade geddon a stylized multiplayer  shooter set in third person our local  arcade has made a super game combining  all the best games in the world into one  but it's been hacked and a virus is  spreading inside you can go alone or  with up to three friends to jump in and  save the day the game is split into  different biomes which are procedurally  generated so every time you do jump in  it should feel different the plan for  arcadergedon is to house different game  modes over time but at its core it's a  pve survival horde mode we pick up  missions from vendors and jump into the  game to complete them rinse and repeat  it's sort of like a roguelike every time  you jump back in everything you had on a  previous run is totally gone over the  last 12 months new biomes weapons and  bosses have been added as well as many  pvp modes for those who don't want to  game against endless ai arguably the pvp  minigames are better than the core mode  illfonic regularly updates the roadmap  for arcade again and more modes are  coming on release so the question is  will you try it so that's our month  those on ps plus extra i'm trying to  decide how to cover that content stray  will be the first day-and-date release  coming to that tier later this month  depending on how regularly that tier is  updated i'll showcase new arrivals in  another video i'm adam you're awesome  i'll see you next time  [Music]

